@startuml
title simpletickr auth — local vs OIDC

actor Browser
participant "SecurityConfig\n(filter chain)" as SC
participant AuthController as AC
participant AuthUserDetailsService as UDS
participant OidcConnectController as OC
participant "Spring OAuth2 filters\n(authorization redirect +\ncallback + token exchange)" as OF
participant "IdP (external)" as IdP
participant OidcAuthenticationSuccessHandler as SH
participant "ResolveOrProvisionOidcUserUseCase /\nConnectOidcIdentityUseCase" as UC
participant SessionPrincipalEstablisher as SPE
participant OidcTokenRefreshFilter as TR
database "Session\n(Postgres, Spring Session JDBC)" as DB

== Local login ==
Browser -> AC: POST /auth/login (username, password)
AC -> UDS: authenticationManager.authenticate(...)
UDS --> AC: LocalUserDetails (password OK)
AC -> SPE: establish(Principal.Local)
SPE -> DB: rotate session id, save SecurityContext
AC --> Browser: 200 + Set-Cookie: SESSION

== OIDC login (fresh) ==
Browser -> OF: GET /oauth2/authorization/oidc
OF -> IdP: 302 redirect (Authorization Code + PKCE)
Browser -> IdP: user authenticates there
IdP -> OF: 302 /login/oauth2/code/oidc?code=...
OF -> OF: exchange code for tokens,\nvalidate ID token
OF -> SH: onAuthenticationSuccess(OidcUser)
SH -> UC: execute(claims)
UC --> SH: User (existing, or auto-provisioned)
SH -> SPE: establish(Principal.Oidc)
SPE -> DB: rotate session id, save SecurityContext
SH --> Browser: 302 to frontend "/"

== OIDC connect (adds SSO to an already-logged-in local user) ==
note over Browser: already authenticated as Principal.Local
Browser -> OC: GET /auth/oidc/connect
OC -> DB: session.setAttribute(connectUserId)
OC --> Browser: 302 /oauth2/authorization/oidc
Browser -> OF: (same IdP round trip as above)
OF -> SH: onAuthenticationSuccess(OidcUser)
SH -> DB: read + clear connectUserId
SH -> UC: execute(connectUserId, claims)
SH -> SPE: establish(Principal.Local) — same user,\nnow with an OIDC identity linked
SH --> Browser: 302 /settings/security?oidcConnected=true

== Every later request ==
Browser -> SC: any request, Cookie: SESSION
SC -> DB: load SecurityContext\n(principal is Local or Oidc)
SC -> TR: (only acts if principal is Principal.Oidc)
TR -> IdP: refresh access token, only if stale
TR --> SC: ok, or invalidate session\nif the IdP rejects the refresh
SC -> "target controller": currentUser()
@enduml
